[Event "Intermediate tactics: deflection, the lesson"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Role "teaching"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/cB9DXF3Y/eBDFn8CO"]
[FEN "r1q3k1/4bppp/pp2pn2/4B3/8/2N2Q2/PPPR1PPP/6K1 b - - 0 18"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1q3k1/4bppp/pp2pn2/4B3/8/2N2Q2/PPPR1PPP/6K1_b_-_-_0_18"]

{ Welcome to intermediate tactics. Today's trick is deflection: pull a defender away from its post, and whatever it was guarding falls. } 18... Nd7 { His knight drops back to d seven, and only the queen still watches the rook tucked away on a eight. Take the knight there and she has to answer. [%cal Yd2d7][%csl Rc8,Ra8] } 19. Rxd7 { His queen is the only thing guarding the rook on a eight. Now she must take. [%cal Rc8a8] } (19. Bd4 { A lovely square for the bishop, but the guard keeps her job. } 19... Bf6 20. h3 h6 21. a4 Bxd4 { A level game, and the trick has gone. }) (19. Bd6 { You trade bishops and forget the deflection. } 19... Bxd6 20. Rxd6 Rb8 21. Qe4 Qc7 { Equal. Nothing happened here. }) 19... Qxd7 { She had to take, and now nobody is watching a eight. [%csl Ra8] } 20. Qxa8+ { Check, and a whole rook. His queen was the only piece watching a eight, and the check keeps her away for good. That is deflection: pull the guard away, then take what is left. } (20. Bxg7 { A free pawn while a rook hangs in the corner. } 20... Rd8 21. Bh6 Qd4 22. g3 Qf6 { You gave a rook for a knight and got nothing. }) (20. h4 { A quiet move, and the whole point disappears. } 20... Rd8 21. a3 f6 22. Bf4 b5 { The rook walked away and you are worse. }) 1-0


[Event "Intermediate tactics: deflection with a check"]
