{ His queen is about to wander onto a square where she will have two jobs at once. } 13... Qxb2 { She grabs the pawn on b two, but she is still meant to be watching your knight on e five too. } 14. Bd4 { The bishop steps into the diagonal. She cannot see e five any more. [%cal Rb2e5] } (14. Rxf6 { You grab a knight and he takes back with the pawn. } 14... gxf6 15. Nf4 Qa3 16. Bd4 Qe7 { Equal, and your rook has gone. }) (14. a3 { You defend and hand him a free move. } 14... Ba6 15. Bd4 Bxe2 16. Bxb2 Bxd1 { Everything comes off. }) 14... Qa3 { The queen has to run. What was she looking after? [%csl Ra3] } 15. Bxe5 { A free knight. Standing your bishop on the diagonal is interference — her line to e five is gone, so you collect. } (15. Rxf6 { The other knight, and the wrong one. } 15... gxf6 16. Nf4 c5 17. dxc6 dxc6 { Level. The e five knight was free. }) (15. Rf5 { You attack again with a piece hanging. } 15... d6 16. Rxf6 gxf6 17. Nf4 f5 { You had a whole knight. }) 1-0


