{ New trick: the in between move. Before you recapture, look for a stronger move the position cannot ignore. } 30. Nxf4 { His knight grabs your bishop on f four. Do not take back yet — check first. [%cal Yg6e4] } Qe4+ { Check! Taking back can wait one move. He has to answer this. [%csl Rh1] } (30... Rxf4 { The automatic recapture, straight away. } 31. Rxf4 Qxc2 32. Qf2 Qg6 { He took back with tempo and now you are the one losing. }) (30... Qxc2 { You grab the other knight and lose the thread. } 31. Qd4 Qxb2 32. Nxh3 a5 { His attack is much faster. }) (30... Qxg4 { A pawn, with a piece hanging on f four. } 31. Ne3 Qxf4 32. Rxf4 Rxf4 { You are a piece down. }) 31. Kg1 { He has nowhere else to hide from the check. } Rxf4 { Now you take. The in between check gained a tempo, and the knight never got a chance to run. } (31... Qxc2 { You take the wrong knight and let the other one live. } 32. Qf2 Qxf2+ 33. Rxf2 d4 { Everything falls apart. }) (31... a5 { A slow move with a knight hanging. } 32. Rae1 Qxc2 33. Nxh3 Rxf1+ { The moment has gone. }) 0-1


